  "summary": "New benchmarks expose how well methods predict EC numbers, enzyme catalysis, gene essentiality and causal structure in kinetic networks, including with latent variables.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is benchmarking and model development for inferring enzyme function and metabolic network behavior. MCDBench provides 792 medium-chain dehydrogenase enzyme-substrate-cofactor combinations, including validated inactives, to compare four predictors of catalytic performance. A systematic review benchmarks EC number prediction from reaction chemical structures, comparing similarity-based and ML/deep learning approaches. HyperGenie applies directed hypergraph neural networks to genome-scale metabolic models to predict bacterial gene essentiality from wild-type flux features. A fourth preprint evaluates temporal causal discovery methods (tMIIC, PCMCI+/LPCMCI, SVAR-FCI) on simulated kinetic networks with latent confounders. The items are heterogeneous: three address enzyme or metabolic prediction, while the causal discovery work concerns network inference more generally. What is new is the emphasis on curated negatives, comparative metrics and partial observability.",
